    "narrative": "For today\u2019s slate, our offensive core is headlined by **Brice Turang** (75.06) and **Corbin Carroll** (73.47). **Brice Turang** benefits immensely from a soft matchup against Merrill Kelly (5.47 xERA), and his position in the three-hole, combined with a 19% boost from the opposing SP\u2019s lack of effectiveness, makes him our top efficiency play. Meanwhile, **Corbin Carroll** remains a priority start; despite a tougher matchup against Brandon Woodruff, the 100% stolen base potential against this specific battery and his favorable spot in the order keep his floor high for our scarcest category. **Josh Naylor** (70.49) is our other anchor, feasting on Bieber\u2019s 5.52 xERA, which provides the largest single SP-skill boost in our lineup.\n\nThe most difficult decision on the bench was **Alex Freeland**, who posted a 49.35 score, narrowly missing the cut behind the utility slot occupied by **Austin Riley**. While **Alex Freeland** offers switch-hitting versatility, his projected ninth-order slot proved to be the anchor that kept him out of the starting nine, as we prioritized the structural lineup placement of our starters. We are closely monitoring **Travis Bazzana** (52.20) due to a 37% rain risk; if the game is postponed, we will need to pivot quickly to maintain our daily efficiency targets. Additionally, while **Mickey Moniak** (69.94) carries a strong score, fantasy managers should note that his platoon disadvantage against Robbie Ray is only partially mitigated by a favorable park factor, making his start a high-variance play for today. \n\nAs always, keep an eye on official lineups for **Dalton Rushing**, **Gabriel Moreno**, **Max Muncy**, **Kyle Karros**, **Mickey Moniak**, **Corbin Carroll**, **Seiya Suzuki**, and **Austin Riley**. We have built this lineup to maximize production across all categories, and while players like **James Wood** carry a lower score (51.23) due to a matchup with a tougher arm in Ashcraft, his elite xwOBA metrics justify the start as we look to capitalize on his high-upside profile. **Zach McKinstry** rounds out our outfield as a necessary efficiency play, though we remain ready to slot in reserves if weather impacts our primary targets.",
